cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PixelFlow in your work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: PixelFlow
abstract: >-
  PixelFlow is a web application for building image-processing pipelines
  visually. Users chain operations from OpenCV, scikit-image and Pillow
  (77 built-in operations plus user-defined convolution kernels), preview
  a single image live with incremental recomputation, and run pipelines
  over many images as background jobs. The operation library is declared
  once in a schema-driven backend registry (FastAPI, Python) from which the
  React/TypeScript frontend renders every control, including interactive
  point, region and colour picks. Pipelines can be saved, reused as custom
  filters and shared by link.
authors:
  - alias: Mauryantitans
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mauryantitans/PixelFlow"
